  <XDFPATCH uniqueid="0x1144">
    <title>[PATCH] True manual</title>
    <description>True manual. Removes the TCU-side forced upshift at redline: 0x1CECA4/0x1CECA6 -> 0xFFFF (stock 7100/6825 rpm) kills guard test 1 in FUN_0012c9b8; the DME limiter still protects the engine. R2: 0xFF over 0x1D3A80/81 (df32 seeds, stock 105) and 0xFFFF over 0x1D28EC (rev-match latch arm, stock 6500 rpm). R3: 00 over 0x1D34B1 (df31 gate threshold in FUN_0012c660, stock 02); hinges on runtime def4 - supervised test only (program patch 0x12CA44/56 is the deterministic fix). APPLY ORDER: Stage 3 maps first, then this as pure overwrite (no basedata); recompute the CRC after all patches. R4: 0x1CC03C cap 7200->10000 (test 2). R5: K0 lever (e_work/notes/tm_round5.md): fills strat_state_attr_3[100] 0x1C927C..0x1C92DF with 01 -> dd39!=0 -> df31=1 -> test-2 threshold (da9c*df32)/100 becomes 2.55x (df32=255); the ~7200 forced upshift cannot fire.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="1" />
    <XDFPATCHENTRY name="overspeed_limit_1" address="0x1CECA4" datasize="0x2" patchdata="FFFF" />
    <XDFPATCHENTRY name="overspeed_limit_2" address="0x1CECA6" datasize="0x2" patchdata="FFFF" />
    <XDFPATCHENTRY name="overspeed_margin_a" address="0x1D3A80" datasize="0x1" patchdata="FF" />
    <XDFPATCHENTRY name="overspeed_margin_b" address="0x1D3A81" datasize="0x1" patchdata="FF" />
    <XDFPATCHENTRY name="revmatch_latch_arm" address="0x1D28EC" datasize="0x2" patchdata="FFFF" />
    <XDFPATCHENTRY name="df31_gate_off" address="0x1D34B1" datasize="0x1" patchdata="00" />
    <XDFPATCHENTRY name="strat_state_attr_3_01" address="0x1C927C" datasize="0x64" patchdata="01010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101" />
  </XDFPATCH>
  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x11B1" flags="0x0">
    <title>Radumfang - dynamic wheel circumference (mm)</title>
    <description>Dynamic wheel circumference in mm - the tyre's ROLLING circumference, not the geometric one.
Formula: pi x (rim_inch x 25.4 + 2 x width_mm x profile_pct/100) x 0.97
Worked example: 225/45R17 = 1933 mm.
If the tyre maker publishes a rolling circumference (Abrollumfang), use that value directly.
IMPORTANT: after flashing, reset the learned rear axle value (Tool32 job steuern_lernfkt_ruecksetzen, argument 0) and drive above ~24 km/h so it re-learns. Then read status_lernfkt: the learned value must equal your real diff ratio; if it is one step off (e.g. 3.91 instead of 3.73), multiply your entry by (real ratio / learned value) and repeat.
Note: the TCU only accepts the closest value from its fixed ratio list (2.00 2.35 2.47 2.56 2.65 2.81 2.93 3.08 3.15 3.23 3.38 3.46 3.64 3.73 3.91 4.10 4.27), so the entry only needs to be within about -1 %/+2.5 % of the reference.
Do not use this to correct the speedometer - that is the DSC's coding.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="1" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x00" mmedaddress="0x195F10" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
    <decimalpl>0</decimalpl>
    <datatype>0</datatype>
    <unittype>0</unittype>
    <DALINK index="0" />
